:PNLGRP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME=RTVSPLFA.Retrieve SPLF Attributes - Help
:P.This command was created to retrieve a spooled files attributes.
It allows one, many or all attributes to be retrieved.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='RTVSPLFA/SPLF'.Spool File Name - HELP
:XH3.SPLF - Spool File Name
:P.Enter the name of the spool file to retrieve attrbiutes for.
:P.Example: QPRINT
:P.This is a required parameter.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='RTVSPLFA/JOB'.Job name (JOB) - Help
:XH3.JOB - Job name
:P.Specifies the job that created the spooled file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*:EPK.
:PD.The job that created the spooled file issued this command.
:PT.:PV.Qualifier 1: Job name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the job that contains the spooled file.
:PT.:PV.Qualifier 2: User:EPV.
:PD.Specify the user name that identifies the user profile under which
the job is run.
:PT.:PV.Qualifier 3: Number:EPV.
:PD.Specify the system-assigned job number.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='RTVSPLFA/SPLNBR'.Spooled file number (SPLNBR) - Help
:XH3.SPLNBR - Spooled file number
:P.Specifies the unique number of the spooled file in the job
whose attributes are being changed.
:P.This is a required parameter.
:P.The possible values are:
:PARML.
:PT.:PK def.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.If there is more than one spooled file with the specified file name
the one with the highest number is the file whose attributes are
changed.
:PT.:PV.*ONLY:EPV.
:PD.Only one spooled file in the job has the specified file name;
therefore, the number of the spooled file is not necessary.
:PT.:PV.1-999999:EPV.
:PD.Specify the number of the spooled file that matches the file name
whose attributes you wish to change.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='RTVSPLFA/FORMTYPE'.Form Type (FORMTYPE) - Help
:XH3.FORMTYPE - Form Type
:P.Specifies a variable to receive the form type. The variable must be
declared as *CHAR LEN(10).
:P.This is an optional parameter.
:EHELP.
